    "body": "This post outlines a hypothetical approach to designing a prompt regression test suite for local LLM experiments. The goal is to establish a repeatable method for evaluating prompt changes without relying on measured results. We propose using a fixed set of 12 test prompts (F1) to ensure consistent evaluation. The core idea is to compare the output of an 'old' prompt set against a 'new' set using identical model configurations (F2). This comparison should cover diverse scenarios, including questions with clear answers and those where information is insufficient (F3). It is crucial to remember that this is a hypothetical experiment design; no actual improvement data is available at this stage (F4). The intention is to create a framework for future, actual testing. We aim to establish a baseline before any modifications are made. This structured approach helps isolate the impact of prompt engineering.",
