    "title": "Designing a Hypothetical Prompt Regression Test for Local LLM Prompt Engineering",
    "body": "This guide details a hypothetical framework for prompt regression testing in a local LLM context. The objective is to create a systematic way to assess prompt modifications. We propose a test suite comprising 12 fixed prompts (F1). The methodology involves evaluating both the existing and proposed new prompts against the same underlying model and settings (F2). This ensures a fair comparison. The test cases should be designed to include a mix of queries that are answerable with the provided context and those that are not, due to insufficient information (F3). It's vital to stress that this is a conceptual exercise and no performance improvements have been measured or confirmed (F4). The focus is on the *design* of the test, not its outcomes. This hypothetical setup aims to provide a reproducible method for prompt validation before any real-world deployment or extensive benchmarking.",
